# PURGED (2026-07-28, ADR-0083, owner-authorized): the replay whitelist that used
# to live here (!logs/runs/*.wav) is gone WITH its history -- git-filter-repo
# removed every audio file from all refs and the rewrite was force-pushed to
# origin and nas. Raw personal voice never enters git again: no negations, no
# exceptions. Replay fixtures must be PII-free, converted to .npy under
# tests/fixture_audio/, and reviewed before `git add -f`. Local session WAVs
# stay on disk (ignored below) and in the owner's offline archive.
logs/runs/**

# Per-run pytest log bundles are transient (timestamped trace + summary for the
# machine they ran on); curated logs/runs/ bundles are committed, these are not.
logs/tests/

# Live-validation run artifacts (tools/live_session): large per-run wavs +
# machine-specific timelines. The analysis lives in docs/, not the raw bundles.
logs/live/

# Real-usage harness per-run reports (tools/real_usage): transient PASS/FAIL
# bundles for one on-machine run. The curated overview is logs/runs/OVERVIEW.md.
logs/real_usage/

# Versioned conversation-gate reports contain fixed synthetic model/tool text
# and machine-specific timing/provenance metadata; keep each run local.
logs/conversation-eval/

# Autonomous test harness (tools/autotest): transient per-run verdicts +
# synthesized inject clips + engine stdout. The voice tier ALSO drops a curated
# run bundle under logs/runs/ (committed via the whitelist above); these are not.
logs/autotest/

# Owner's recorded test clips (tools.autotest record). Raw personal voice -- per
# architecture §9.7 it stays on the device and is NOT committed.
/recordings/

# Jupyter
.ipynb_checkpoints/
*.ipynb

# OS
.DS_Store
Thumbs.db

# Logs
*.log

# Local config (keep config.json as template)
config.local.json
config.local.json.bak*

# Local Claude Code session config (machine-local, never committed)
.claude/

# Environment variables
.env
.env.local

# Claude Code local config: machine-specific autonomy permissions + guard hook
# (hard-codes this machine's paths; not shared). Promote to .claude/settings.json
# with relative paths if you ever want it committed.
.claude/settings.local.json
.claude/hooks/

# Generated test reports (tools/run_tests.py)
test-reports/
# Download/cache root used by real-model sanity and benchmark tooling.
.cache/

# Swarm harness per-run churn; .agents/last_report.json is committed as the
# version verdict snapshot, but the append-only history is local noise.
.agents/history.jsonl

# Accidental cross-machine cruft / stray redirect output. `UsersPaul` was a
# stray GitHub-API 404 body written to a file; `social_media_activities_app/`
# is a SEPARATE project (its own .git) that was once nested here by mistake and
# now lives as a sibling repo -- guard so neither can ever be staged again.
UsersPaul
social_media_activities_app/

# Session-bootstrap briefings (tools/session_bootstrap.py) are machine-local and
# regenerated each session from the committed run-logs/handoff docs.
logs/session_*_bootstrap.md

# Downloaded model weights -- large binaries, NEVER commit. Fetch on each
# machine with `python -m tools.setup_models` (sherpa) or the phone GGUFs.
pretrained_models/sherpa/
# Downloaded sherpa-onnx model bundles (hundreds of MB; fetched on demand).
pretrained_models/sherpa-onnx-*/
# ...including nested staging dirs (e.g. asr_candidates/sherpa-onnx-*/).
pretrained_models/asr_candidates/
pretrained_models/**/sherpa-onnx-*/
models/
*.gguf
tmp/

# Mic-calibration recording sessions (tools/calibration_suite.py): raw voice
# WAVs + free-speech transcripts in summary.json/GRADES.md -- PII, never commit
# (SS 9.7). The *.wav rule above already catches the audio; this catches the rest.
calib_runs/
